== 9.8 Chapter 9 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [A drug is best defined as],
  [any substance that kills bacteria],
  [any medicine sold in a pharmacy],
  [any substance that alters the way the body or mind works],
  [any illegal substance]
)

#mcq(2, [Which of the following is a stimulant?],
  [Heroin],
  [Caffeine],
  [Alcohol],
  [Paracetamol]
)

#mcq(3, [Alcohol is classed as a depressant because it],
  [destroys the liver],
  [slows down the transmission of impulses across synapses],
  [causes cancer],
  [increases the speed of nerve impulses]
)

#mcq(4, [Which drug is used medically to relieve pain?],
  [LSD],
  [Nicotine],
  [Cocaine],
  [Morphine]
)

#mcq(5, [Tolerance to a drug means that],
  [the same dose produces less effect, so a larger dose is needed],
  [the user becomes immune to all drugs],
  [the user can stop without symptoms],
  [the drug is no longer absorbed]
)

#mcq(6, [Withdrawal symptoms occur when],
  [a drug is taken for the first time],
  [the drug is injected rather than swallowed],
  [a dependent person stops taking the drug],
  [the dose is increased]
)

#mcq(7, [An overdose of a depressant drug is dangerous mainly because it],
  [causes a rash],
  [raises the blood pressure],
  [makes the user violent],
  [depresses the centres that control breathing]
)

#mcq(8, [Excessive alcohol damages the liver by causing],
  [anaemia],
  [cirrhosis],
  [scurvy],
  [rickets]
)

#mcq(9, [The harmful substance in cigarette smoke that is most associated with addiction is],
  [tar],
  [carbon monoxide],
  [nicotine],
  [carbon dioxide]
)

#mcq(10, [Carbon monoxide in cigarette smoke is harmful because it],
  [irritates the eyes],
  [stains the teeth],
  [reduces the oxygen-carrying capacity of the blood],
  [causes cancer directly]
)

#mcq(11, [A pregnant woman who drinks heavily risks],
  [immunity for the child],
  [foetal alcohol syndrome in the child],
  [producing twins],
  [a faster delivery]
)

#mcq(12, [The first thing a first-aider should do on reaching an accident scene is to],
  [give the casualty water],
  [check that the scene is safe],
  [move the casualty to hospital],
  [bandage all open wounds]
)

#mcq(13, [In the first-aid priority order, the letters DRABC stand for],
  [Diagnosis, Response, Antiseptic, Breathing, Compression],
  [Drugs, Rest, Air, Bandage, Care],
  [Danger, Recovery, Ambulance, Bleeding, Casualty],
  [Danger, Response, Airway, Breathing, Circulation]
)

#mcq(14, [A casualty who is unconscious but breathing should be],
  [laid on the back with the head raised],
  [given sweet tea],
  [made to sit upright],
  [placed in the recovery position]
)

#mcq(15, [The first aid for a minor burn is to],
  [cool it with clean running water for at least ten minutes],
  [burst the blister],
  [apply oil or toothpaste],
  [cover it with cotton wool]
)

#mcq(16, [In the first aid of a fracture, the limb should be],
  [immobilised with a splint without being straightened],
  [massaged],
  [pulled straight at once],
  [warmed with a hot compress]
)

#mcq(17, [A casualty bleeding heavily from a cut on the arm should first have],
  [the arm held below the heart],
  [a tourniquet tied at once],
  [firm pressure applied with a clean pad],
  [the wound washed with kerosene]
)

#mcq(18, [The first aid for a snake bite is to],
  [keep the casualty still, immobilise the limb and get to hospital],
  [cut the wound and suck out the venom],
  [apply a tight tourniquet and walk fast],
  [give the casualty alcohol]
)

#mcq(19, [Which of the following belongs in a first-aid box?],
  [A stethoscope],
  [Antibiotics for injection],
  [A syringe and a scalpel],
  [Sterile gauze, bandages and antiseptic]
)

#mcq(20, [An unconscious casualty should never be given anything by mouth because],
  [it will cause a fever],
  [it wastes the medicine],
  [the casualty may choke or inhale it into the lungs],
  [it is against the law]
)

#mcq(21, [Public health is best described as],
  [the treatment of individual patients in hospital],
  [the sale of medicines],
  [the study of diseases],
  [the work of keeping a whole community healthy by prevention]
)

#mcq(22, [The most effective single measure against water-borne disease in a village is],
  [a safe water supply and proper sanitation],
  [more doctors],
  [free medicine],
  [a new hospital]
)

#mcq(23, [Which measure most directly controls malaria in a community?],
  [Draining stagnant water and using insecticide-treated nets],
  [Covering food],
  [Boiling drinking water],
  [Vaccinating against measles]
)

#mcq(24, [Health education is important because it],
  [provides free drugs],
  [replaces the need for clean water],
  [cures disease directly],
  [teaches people how to avoid disease and so prevents it]
)

#mcq(25, [A community with open refuse dumps is likely to have an increase in],
  [exclusive breast-feeding],
  [malaria only],
  [flies and the diseases they carry],
  [vitamin C deficiency]
)

#mcq(26, [Which of these is not a class of drug?],
  [Depressant],
  [Antiseptic],
  [Hallucinogen],
  [Stimulant]
)

#mcq(27, [The main social effect of drug abuse is],
  [loss of income, family breakdown and crime],
  [better health],
  [improved school performance],
  [longer life]
)

#mcq(28, [Cannabis is obtained from],
  [the leaves and flowers of Cannabis sativa],
  [the opium poppy],
  [fermented grain],
  [the coca plant]
)

#mcq(29, [Rehabilitation of a drug addict usually involves],
  [no treatment at all],
  [a larger dose of the drug],
  [supervised withdrawal with counselling and support],
  [immediate unsupervised withdrawal at home]
)

#mcq(30, [A person who is dependent on a drug and cannot stop even when he wants to is said to be],
  [addicted],
  [rehabilitated],
  [immune],
  [tolerant]
)

